# Spry and Mighty: "Choose exactly two creatures you control. You draw X cards and the chosen creatures get +X/+X and gain trample
# until end of turn, where X is the difference between the chosen creatures' powers." Bot1 controls Ornithopter (0/2), Elvish
# Mystic (1/1) and Monastery Swiftspear (1/2), and Bot2 a Birds of Paradise: the choice is not targeting (CR 608.2d), but only
# creatures Bot1 controls may be chosen, so the Birds is refused, and so are three creatures: exactly two. Bot1 chooses the Ornithopter and the Mystic: X is 1, so Bot1 draws a
# card, those two get +1/+1 (the Mystic 2/2, the Ornithopter 1/3) and the Swiftspear, not chosen, gets only its own prowess +1/+1 for the sorcery (2/3), not Spry and Mighty's.

